---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How Escrow Works - Qaraye Marchants"
  description="How escrow protects buyers and sellers on Qaraye Marchants. Safe payments for local and cross-border agricultural trade."
>
  <div class="escrow-page">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Home</a>

    <header class="hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Trust &amp; Safety</span>
      <h1>How Escrow Works</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every transaction on Qaraye Marchants can be protected by escrow — a legal
        arrangement where your money is held by a licensed provider until you
        confirm the goods arrived as described.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content">
      <h2>The 5-Step Process</h2>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>1. You choose a product</h3>
          <p>Browse verified listings from merchants across Nigeria. Every listing shows the seller's location, verification status, and full product details.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>2. You pay into escrow</h3>
          <p>Instead of paying the seller directly, you pay a licensed escrow provider. The money leaves your account but is held safely — the seller cannot access it yet.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>3. Seller ships the goods</h3>
          <p>Once the escrow provider confirms your payment, the seller is notified to ship. Both sides see the same shipment tracking.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>4. You confirm delivery</h3>
          <p>When the goods arrive, inspect them. If everything matches the listing, click "Confirm Receipt". If something is wrong, open a dispute within 7 days.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>5. Seller gets paid</h3>
          <p>The escrow provider releases your payment to the seller. If you raised a valid dispute, the funds remain held until the issue is resolved.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>What Escrow Protects You From</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Non-delivery</h3>
          <p>If the seller never ships, you get a full refund. The money never leaves escrow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Wrong items</h3>
          <p>If the goods don't match the description, you can dispute the transaction and keep the funds in escrow until it is resolved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Fake sellers</h3>
          <p>Merchants who take payment and disappear are permanently banned. Their escrow history is reviewed before any new listing is approved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Currency risk</h3>
          <p>For cross-border deals, escrow locks in the exchange rate at the time of payment, so neither party loses out from FX swings.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Fees</h2>
      <p>Escrow protection is charged as a small percentage of the item price. The fee is paid by the buyer on top of the item price.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Item Price (NGN)</th>
            <th>Escrow Fee</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Up to ₦500,000</td><td>2.5% (min ₦2,000)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>₦500,001 – ₦2,000,000</td><td>2.0% (min ₦5,000)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>₦2,000,001 – ₦10,000,000</td><td>1.5% (min ₦15,000)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Above ₦10,000,000</td><td>1.0% (min ₦50,000)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Cross-Border Transactions</h2>
      <p>Qaraye Marchants supports escrow for international buyers too. When you purchase from a Nigerian merchant as an overseas buyer, or vice versa, the same protection applies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Escrow holds the funds in the seller's local currency equivalent</li>
        <li>Payment rails support USD, GBP, EUR, and other major currencies</li>
        <li>Customs documentation and shipping insurance can be bundled in</li>
        <li>Dispute resolution is handled by a neutral third party</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Who holds the money during escrow?</summary>
          <p>Funds are held by a licensed payment provider regulated by the Central Bank of Nigeria. Qaraye Marchants never takes custody of your money.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What if the seller refuses to ship?</summary>
          <p>Open a dispute through your dashboard. The escrow provider will contact the seller. If they cannot prove shipment within 7 days, your payment is refunded in full.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How long does the money stay in escrow?</summary>
          <p>Until you confirm receipt. There is no fixed time limit — but most transactions complete within 5–14 days depending on shipping.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I use escrow for cash-on-delivery?</summary>
          <p>Yes — but cash-on-delivery limits protection. Escrow is always safer because the money is committed before shipping, so the seller has proof of intent to buy.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What about international buyers?</summary>
          <p>Cross-border escrow is supported. Payment is converted at the mid-market rate at the time of the transaction. Refunds are paid back in the buyer's original currency.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="cta">
        <p>Ready to buy safely?</p>
        <a href="/products" class="cta-btn">Browse Products</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .escrow-page {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 24px 80px;
    color: var(--ink, #f0f4ff);
  }
  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--mono, monospace);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8b95b8);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--cyan, #00e5ff); }

  .hero { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono, monospace);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cyan, #00e5ff);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--display, sans-serif);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 10px 0 16px;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8b95b8);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .content h2 {
    font-family: var(--display, sans-serif);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 48px 0 16px;
    padding-left: 14px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--cyan, #00e5ff);
  }
  .content p, .content li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8b95b8);
  }
  .content ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }
  .content ul li { margin: 8px 0; }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 24px 0;
    counter-reset: steps;
  }
  .steps > li {
    background: var(--bg-850, #0f1526);
    border: 1px solid var(--card-border, rgba(0,229,255,0.16));
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .steps h3 {
    font-family: var(--display, sans-serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink, #f0f4ff);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .steps p { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .card {
    background: var(--bg-850, #0f1526);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft, rgba(255,255,255,0.06));
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 20px;
  }
  .card h3 {
    font-family: var(--display, sans-serif);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink, #f0f4ff);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .card p { margin: 0; font-size: 13.5px; }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 20px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  thead th {
    background: var(--bg-850, #0f1526);
    color: var(--cyan, #00e5ff);
    font-family: var(--mono, monospace);
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }
  tbody td {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft, rgba(255,255,255,0.06));
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8b95b8);
  }

  .faq { margin: 20px 0; }
  .faq details {
    background: var(--bg-850, #0f1526);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink, #f0f4ff);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .faq details[open] summary { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .faq p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; }

  .cta {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--bg-850, #0f1526), var(--bg-900, #0a0f1d));
    border: 1px solid var(--cyan, #00e5ff);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 32px;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .cta p {
    font-family: var(--display, sans-serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink, #f0f4ff);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .cta-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--cyan, #00e5ff);
    color: #051018;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 14px 32px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .cta-btn:hover { background: #33ebff; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .escrow-page { padding: 24px 16px 60px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 26px; }
    .content h2 { font-size: 20px; margin-top: 36px; }
  }
</style>